class.description:
[InputIconServer] holds one [InputIconSet] per [enum InputIconFamily] (keyboard and mouse, generic gamepad, Xbox, PlayStation, Nintendo). The sets come from the project settings [code]input_devices/icons/keyboard_mouse[/code], [code]input_devices/icons/generic_gamepad[/code], [code]input_devices/icons/xbox[/code], [code]input_devices/icons/playstation[/code] and [code]input_devices/icons/nintendo[/code] (loaded on first use), or from [method set_icon_set] at runtime.
[method get_icon] picks the family from the event: keys and mouse buttons use [constant INPUT_ICON_FAMILY_KEYBOARD_MOUSE]; gamepad events use [member gamepad_family] if it is set, else the family of the event's device (joypad name and vendor id), else, for events of all devices, the family of the first connected gamepad, else [constant INPUT_ICON_FAMILY_GENERIC_GAMEPAD].
The editor's Input Map uses the same icons when they are set and the theme icons otherwise.
[codeblocks]
[gdscript]
func _ready():
    InputIconServer.icon_set_changed.connect(_update_prompt)
    _update_prompt(InputIconServer.INPUT_ICON_FAMILY_AUTO)

func _update_prompt(_family):
    var events = InputMap.action_get_events("jump")
    if not events.is_empty():
        $Prompt.texture = InputIconServer.get_icon(events[0])
[/gdscript]
[csharp]
public override void _Ready()
{
    InputIconServer.IconSetChanged += family => UpdatePrompt();
    UpdatePrompt();
}

private void UpdatePrompt()
{
    var events = InputMap.ActionGetEvents("jump");
    if (events.Count > 0)
    {
        GetNode<TextureRect>("Prompt").Texture = InputIconServer.GetIcon(events[0]);
    }
}
[/csharp]
[/codeblocks]
[b]Note:[/b] No icon images are shipped with the engine; a project brings its own.
